sequenceDiagram
    participant C1 as Client (Tab 1 - pay 80k)
    participant C2 as Client (Tab 2 - pay 90k)
    participant PS as Payment Service
    participant US as User Service
    participant DB as User DB (balance = 100k)

    par Request 1 arrives first
        C1->>PS: POST /transactions (amount=80000)
        PS->>US: reserve & deduct balance (userId, 80000)
        US->>DB: BEGIN TRANSACTION
        US->>DB: SELECT balance FROM users WHERE id=? FOR UPDATE
        Note over DB: Row is now LOCKED.<br/>Request 2 must wait here.
        DB-->>US: balance = 100000
        US->>US: check 100000 >= 80000 → OK
        US->>DB: UPDATE balance = 100000 - 80000 = 20000
        US->>DB: COMMIT
        Note over DB: Lock released.
        US-->>PS: 200 OK (new balance = 20000)
        PS-->>C1: 201 Created - transaction success
    and Request 2 arrives almost same time
        C2->>PS: POST /transactions (amount=90000)
        PS->>US: reserve & deduct balance (userId, 90000)
        US->>DB: SELECT balance FROM users WHERE id=? FOR UPDATE
        Note over US,DB: BLOCKED - waiting for<br/>Request 1's lock to release
        DB-->>US: balance = 20000 (after Request 1 committed)
        US->>US: check 20000 >= 90000 → FAIL
        US-->>PS: 409 Conflict - insufficient balance
        PS-->>C2: 409 Conflict - "Số dư không đủ"
    end

    Note over C1,DB: Result: only Request 1 succeeds.<br/>Final balance = 20000 (correct, never negative)
